{
  "name": "How to Prep Your Home for Interior Painting",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Getting your home ready for an interior painting project can seem daunting, but breaking it down makes it much easier. You’re essentially setting the stage for a smooth, high-quality finish. First, move all your furniture away from the walls and cover it with plastic sheeting or drop cloths. You’ll also want to protect your floors thoroughly with drop cloths to catch any drips. Next, remove all hardware from your walls, like switch plates, outlet covers, and light fixtures. If you can, take down curtains and blinds too. Now, it's time for surface preparation: clean your walls to remove any dust or grime. Look for any cracks or nail pops and make sure to patch those up. Don’t forget to sand any patched areas smooth once they’re dry. A good painter will handle most of these details, including taping and caulking, but a little pre-work from you helps everything run efficiently. When you’re dealing with a lived-in space, the pros at HH Remodeling LLC always take extra care to protect your belongings and ensure daily cleanup.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
